<p>The sliding window technique is a subset of the two-pointer pattern, as =
it uses two pointers (generally left and right) to define the bounds of a "=
window" in iterable data structures like arrays. The window defines a subco=
mponent of the data structure (e.g., a subarray or substring), and it <em>s=
lides</em> across the data structure unidirectionally, typically searching =
for a subcomponent that meets a certain requirement.</p>
