inting arrow connects 'left' to the leftmost dot within the window, and a s=
imilar arrow connects 'right' to the rightmost dot within the window.  A li=
ght-blue upward-pointing arrow labeled 'window' indicates that this window =
can move along the sequence.  The arrangement visually demonstrates how the=
 window's position is controlled by the 'left' and 'right' pointers, allowi=
ng it to slide across the data sequence, processing a fixed-size subset at =
a time." loading=3D"lazy" width=3D"244" height=3D"81" decoding=3D"async" da=
